silm:instances_papers_05_granite_substrate_chapters_05_absorption_law_sections_02_profile_preservation_concrete_anchor#profilepreservationsymbol silm:hasLongDescription "The ProfilePreservationSymbol is Profile preservation: after absorbing a source text about Mittens through alpha, the Yoneda profile of the absorbed olog node must agree with Hom(-,Mittens) restricted to the legs the text supports. The vet-record text supports the evidence leg; after absorption, the evidence-leg node must have the same Hom-profile as the vet-record chunk." .
